{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1290802-mage-bloodbowl-op-starting-characters","id":1290802,"title":"Mage Bloodbowl; \"OP\" starting characters","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-02-22T09:35:38-08:00","id":1290802,"title":"Mage Bloodbowl; \"OP\" starting characters","content":"This is just for fun. If you like crunch and exploring mechanics, then enjoy the thread. If you don't like this sort of mechanical tweaking/min-maxing then that's fine. Just submit a dumb/broken/OP concept and come up with ideas to make the other concepts even more broken.<br /> <br /> RULES:<br /> <br /> - Standard M20 character creation. However we're going to assume that all &quot;optional&quot; mechanics and setups are turned on. All merits can be purchased, that sort of thing. Let's just assume you took 13 points of flaws you damned munchkin, for 28 freebie points. If a flaw is important to the character's OP powers then mention it in the writeup.<br /> <br /> - No Marauders, since there are mechanical upsides and they come for &quot;&quot;&quot;free&quot;&quot;&quot;. Also worth noting that M20 doesn't give us creation rules for Marauder PCs.<br /> <br /> - Remember that mind control isn't going to be over in a single roll unless your target is some sort of spineless thrall or sub-standard mook. Mind can be incredibly potent, but when it comes to ending an encounter without throwing a single blow... Dominate it ain't. Then again I might be wrong, and it might be possible to <b><i>consistently</i></b> take another mage out in the first round or two with Mind 3. It would be interesting to see.<br /> <br /> - This isn't going to be a total white room. If a concept demands approaching stealthily, observing the target and striking when they least expect it, then cool. If your concept demands the use of spirits then you won't be somewhere with Gauntlet 10 (although the fact that you're weaker with a higher Gauntlet is something to keep in mind of course).<br /> <br /> - Unless you have some cool way of overcoming space/weight limitations (like using Correspondence or a Wonder to pull whatever gear you need out of your base), then it's worth remembering that there are only so many Prime 2 Forces 3 Charms you can carry and deploy... for example. If all else is equal, innate trumps dependent.<br /> <br /> - Allies, Retainers, Backup etc. are off-limits simply because &quot;I have my five bodyguards dogpile my opponents&quot; is kinda cheesy. However &quot;with my Mind and Charisma and cop badge it's very easy to get a crowd to attack people&quot; is fair.<br /> <br /> - You're allowed to argue that something is powerful because it can grow in power very efficiently. &quot;And with 8 EXP they'll be able to-&quot; is something valid to consider.<br /> <br /> - It has to fit within some form of Paradigm, naturally.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar6606_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"6606\" data-vbnamecard=\"6606\">Ambrosia</a> thanks for tips on designing rules","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11620,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","user":"twig","date":". 02-22-2019, 02:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-22T11:10:00-08:00","id":1290836,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1290802-mage-bloodbowl-op-starting-characters#post1290802\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- Standard M20 character creation. However we're going to assume that all &quot;optional&quot; mechanics and setups are turned on. All merits can be purchased, that sort of thing. Let's just ignore Flaws since picking out irrelevant flaws with no impact on combat up to the 7/13 point max is pretty simple. So standard dots plus 15 freebies.</div> </div> </div> </div>What kind of munchkin wouldn't pick up irrelevant flaws with no impact on combat? Having more than 15 freebies it's pretty standard in these builds...<br /> <br /> However M20 has something even better that, I think, could make you reconsider the &quot;no flaws policy&quot;. <i>There are some flaws that are quite an advantage in combat</i>:<br /> In particular I'm thinking on:<br /> <br /> *<u>Taint of Corruption</u>(5 points):<br /> Ideal for an infernal Nephilim (which it's quite an advantageous Merit), it makes you &quot;an evil force of evil&quot; (in a way others, like Werewolves, can recognize). It's not something one would want to live with but it grants you a<b> -2 to any work of &quot;malignant magick&quot;</b> (in exchange for a +2 penalty to &quot;good magick&quot;). Since this is about munchkinism, I think that &quot;malignant magick&quot; it's really the way to go: you want to hurt your enemies to win fights, no?.<br /> <br /> <u>*Phylactery</u>(7 points):<br /> <br /> Yes, having your Avatar in a trinket does mean thay you can be disarmed from your magick (but note that a Correspondence effect can <i>always</i> be casted to retrieve it, and a single success it's enough to &quot;contact it&quot; in order to use magick trough it)...however, the &quot;&quot;&quot;&quot;Defect&quot;&quot;&quot;&quot; also states that if your body it's destroyed your soul <b><i>and consciousness</i></b> still lives on the object. More importantly: <b>you can still cast spells in this state</b> (this much it's explicitly stated).<br /> <br /> Of course, Focusing may be a problem, but that's why you will make an Arete 3 mystic and overcome the main Instrument you use for kick-assing purposes.<br /> <br /> <b>Combine this with Immortal Merit</b> (7 points, cancelled by those of the Phylactery) <b>and you have a body that only dies if it's troughly destroyed</b> (of faces a &quot;doom&quot; of your choice that your enemies don't need to know, and may well be the destruction of your Phylactery for a D&amp;D Lich feel), <b>and a mind that can, </b>in theory,<b> keep magically punching your enemies at 0 HP </b><i>because</i> <i>you keep your consciousness </i>(add some Sphere at 1 to see your enemies and you're done)...this will make that &quot;trough destruction&quot; a bit more challenging<br /> <br /> Unless they remove or destroy the Phylactery. However, nothing impedes your Phylactery from being something very hard to break.<br /> <br /> This awesome idea it's even covered in Book of Secrets: And the book basically says, <i>OK, go for it</i>...In fact, that's supposed to be the reason of why mages make phylacteries. Just make sure to have at least Correspondence 2 if you don't want to be Sauron-ed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 02-22-2019, 02:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-22T11:21:01-08:00","id":1290842,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Tiger's Fist</b></span><br /> <br /> tl;dr son of Tiger has Aggravated claws, is spec'd into clawing things.<br /> <br /> <b>Attributes:</b> Physical Primary. Even spread for best results, or min-max to minimize EXP cost.<br /> <br /> <b>Abilities:</b><br /> <br /> - Martial Arts (a specialized form based upon the use of the Bagh Nakh, a &quot;claw&quot; weapon that rests in your palm).<br /> <br /> - Do 1 or 2, to get the Well Trained Advantage.<br /> <br /> - Athletics.<br /> <br /> - Stealth.<br /> <br /> <b>Merits:</b> Nephilim, representing being the son of Tiger, or some tiger deity. There are a lot of benefits to this, but one is that for a Derangement he gets 7 points in Advantages. For 6 points he gets Claws that do Strength + 2 Aggravated. 1 point of rapid healing. Beyond this, 7 points of Quintessence a day is very good. The extra Res/Syn means that once per story you can throw in an extra 4 dice to an Arete or ability roll.<br /> <br /> Now before we factor in magick he's rolling Dex + Martial Arts difficulty 5 to do Strength + 2 Aggravated damage. This is already pretty neat.<br /> <br /> <b>Backgrounds: </b>By taking Tiger as a Totem with our 7 Background points and 1 Freebie we get Totem 4 which gives us +3 to Martial Arts. 3 in Avatar, leaving us with 11 freebies.<br /> <br /> <b>Spheres: </b>Entropy 1 for reducing the difficulty of the Damage roll, Correspondence 2 for clawing from afar, otherwise as preferred. Mind 1 is always a good investment and fits a martial arts paradigm. Same goes for Life 2.<br /> <br /> <b>Arete:</b> 8 freebies give Arete 3, since the dice pool is just very useful. 3 freebies left.<br /> <br /> <b>Finishing touches:</b> 2 freebies pushes us to Martial Arts 4, which means we get a spec, which means more damage with claws. 1 freebie point into Willpower.<br /> <br /> EDIT so with an extra 13 freebies, we're gonna invest in Arcane 5 (because of course we are) leaving 8, and put dots into Melee and Stealth to put them both up to 5.<br /> <br /> So for example, with Dex 4 and Martial Arts 5, with the +3 from Tiger, means 12 dice in an attack roll. Rolling at Difficulty 5 (no magick) or difficulty 2 (magick with quintessence spent and maybe Willpower) we get 7.3 or 9.6 successes... well something above 9.6 anyways, the chart I'm using is great but has 3 as the minimum difficulty.<br /> <br /> So if we go with roughly 7 successes on average (what we'd get without magick), and assume our target will get 3 successes on dodge, that gives 4 successes, with +3 dice to damage.<br /> <br /> Strength of 4, damage bonus of 3, claws give +2. 9 dice of damage against difficulty 6 (pretty sure well trained advantage doesn't apply since the damage step isn't the maneuver). That's 4 aggravated, which isn't bad, but we can do a lot better. With a bit of preparation we can use Entropy 1 to reduce the difficulty of this step. At difficulties 3, 4 and 5 the damage becomes 6.3, 5.5 and 4.7 respectively. This means that with one point of Willpower, some Quintessence and a good roll we can one-shot someone with 7 health points, which covers almost all mages.<br /> <br /> If we're able to ambush, then we roll Dexterity + Stealth + Arcane (14 dice) against difficulty 6, opposed by the target's Perception + Alertness. If we get more than 1 success then we get extra dice to the original attack. Assuming we get 5 successes (which is below average) and our target gets 2, then we get +2 dice to the attack roll. So that's 8.4 successes on attack, leaving 5 successes with 3 dodge, giving +4 dice to damage. 10 against difficulty 3 is 7 damage, so it will give an insta-kill 50% of the time assuming an even distribution.<br /> <br /> <b>Conclusion:</b> sneak attack with this build for a 50% chance of an insta-kill, with one magick effect preparing the turn before. Spend Willpower on the damage roll to all but guarantee an instant death.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11620,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","user":"twig","date":". 02-22-2019, 02:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-22T11:43:17-08:00","id":1290855,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1290802-mage-bloodbowl-op-starting-characters?p=1290836#post1290836\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What kind of munchkin wouldn't pick up irrelevant flaws with no impact on combat? Having more than 15 freebies it's pretty standard in these builds...<br /> <br /> However M20 has something even better that, I think, could make you reconsider the &quot;no flaws policy&quot;. <i>There are some flaws that are quite an advantage in combat</i>:<br /> <br /> *<u>Taint of Corruption</u>(5 points):<br /> Ideal for an infernal Nephilim (which it's quite an advantageous Merit), it makes you &quot;an evil force of evil&quot; (in a way others, like Werewolves, can recognize). It's not something one would want to live with but it grants you a<b> -2 to any work of &quot;malignant magick&quot;</b> (in exchange for a +2 penalty to &quot;good magick&quot;). Since this is about munchkinism, I think that &quot;malignant magick&quot; it's really the way to go: you want to hurt your enemies to win fights, no?.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a good point actually. In that case I could just go back and say &quot;we're assuming you've taken irrelevant flaws to get up to 13 points, just go ahead. If the flaw is helping you in some way say what it is.&quot;<br /> <br /> And yes that taint of corruption spell looks really nasty. Worth remembering that +2 difficulty to good magick means +2 difficulty to healing yourself arguably. Still a really busted flaw!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-22T11:57:48-08:00","id":1290861,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1290802-mage-bloodbowl-op-starting-characters?p=1290836#post1290836\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Immortal Phylactery Mage</div> </div> </div> </div>I get the impression that Immortal can be overhyped. With the Matter sphere you're left in some newly wet cement, with Spirit you're left to assimilate and become one of the umbrood. It's only going to help you against brutes with no problem solving skills, or if you have allies who can rescue you while you're &quot;downed&quot;.<br /> <br /> However the ability to continue making potshots via your Phylactery is very cool, and could make up for this certainly. I know that Arcane would help any build because it's a broken background, but I think it would help a lot here. People are much more likely to forget the body on the floor with Arcane, and less likely to try and destroy their weird ring.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-22T17:37:31-08:00","id":1290940,"title":"","content":"Okay so having read Taint of Corruption from start to finish all I'm getting is that Nephandi, and mages who practice Maleficia, can perform practically all their magick at -2 difficulty in exchange for 7 freebies... as in GAINING freebies. Those 7 points buy you Laham and now you're the son of S A T A N or something edgy like that. You're a mage who wears black and red and uses a gun and says &quot;damn&quot; and isn't anything like that blue mage that runs fast.<br /> <br /> Anyways the -2 difficulty is definitely applying to curses, horrible mind control, offensive magick in general really. It's not as though difficulty reductions are RARE in mage, but consider that you often face difficulty increases. Getting down to -3 from +3 difficulty can take a lot of contributions put together.<br /> <br /> With that in mind, a Nephandus with 5 points in Hypnotism, Mind 3, and Charisma 5. Enchanting (even hypnotic) eyes and voice with the correct merit. Hypnotism in the style of Dr Orwell in a Series of Unfortunate Events. Control people under the guise of being a medical professional (easily done with Mind to help the effect along).<br /> <br /> Taint of Corruption gives -2 difficulty to everything... what Spheres do you need to cover it up? Prime 2 for resonance and Spirit 2 for aura and general soul corruption?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11620,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","user":"twig","date":". 02-22-2019, 08:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-24T15:03:48-08:00","id":1291625,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Taser</b></span><br /> <br /> tl;dr coincidental methods like tasers and guns for Aggravated assaults.<br /> <br /> <b>Attributes:</b> Physical Primary. Even spread for best results, or min-max to minimize EXP cost. Strength can be ignored.<br /> <br /> <b>Abilities:</b><br /> <br /> - Firearms<br /> <br /> - Alertness<br /> <br /> - Athletics<br /> <br /> - Science/Crafts for explosives like grenades<br /> <br /> - Gunsmithing for when Prime 4 eventually lets you make gun wonders... plus making your own guns or tweaking them means -1 difficulty to all those effects<br /> <br /> - Technology, ditto but with tasers<br /> <br /> <b>Merits:</b> Hands of Daedalus for tinkering with and reworking instruments. Essentially -1 difficulty to all effects, as long as the equipment is stuff you've used before.<br /> <br /> <b>Backgrounds: </b>Avatar 5, Resources 2. Invest Resources 1 in two different level 2 &quot;Primal Ventures&quot;, and now you're getting around 20 quintessence a week from your monetary investments.<br /> <br /> <b>Spheres: </b>Forces 2 for amplifying the damage from an attack with a taser, stun gun, firearm... Primal Utility 2 to inflict Aggravated damage and make Charms like Grenades. Primal Utility is trumping Prime for access to nearly infinite Nodes. Mind 1 is good for buffing perception for Aiming, which is a great way to increase damage and pull off impossible shots.<br /> <br /> <b>Arete:</b> 8 freebies give Arete 3, since the dice pool is just very useful.<br /> <br /> <b>Finishing touches:</b> Remaining freebies into Firearms, and backgrounds to represent access to all the relevant kit.<br /> <br /> Now with Dexterity 5 and Firearms 5, we do come to a big question; when we use Forces 2 to amplify the velocity of a bullet, and Prime 2 to charge all the bullets with Quintessence (1 per shot, hence investing so much into Primal Utility for rapid refills with Currency/Quintessence), do we add the extra damage on top of the bullet's ordinary damage? I can't get a 100% clear answer from M20 currently.<br /> <br /> So with Prime 2 alone we're rolling our 10 dice at difficulty 6 (although it could be as low as 3 and as high as 10 depending on the shot), with a spec, for 5.2 successes. We can always boost our successes by having a relevant Technocratic Totem (with Spirit 1 to justify it), since we have many freebies left over. That could give up to 3 bonus dice to Firearms... not that I'd personally agree to a player making up a new Totem that happens to boost Firearms for them. Assuming 13 dice, that's 6.6 successes. With dodge we might end up with 4 successes, so standard damage + 3. Standard revolver is 4 dice of damage, so that's 7 dice of damage 3 times in one turn thanks to the rate of 3.<br /> <br /> 3.2 Aggravated damage, 3 times. So on average dealing 9.6 Aggravated damage. However I may have misunderstood how firearms damage works in M20, feel free to correct me.<br /> <br /> If we go further we can apply a Forces 2 effect after energizing to increase velocity. Then we're looking at 3 dice against difficulty 5 (coincidental), for a 2 success average. That's 6 points of damage per shot that hits... so whether or not we actually apply the damage of the normal Firearms result seems moot. At least M20 tells me in an example that each shot gets the extra damage. And it's not like anyone is soaking 6 Aggravated three times in a row.<br /> <br /> <b>Conclusion:</b> Dealing magickal damage with a firearm might actually be completely broken, in a way that concerns me since pulling it off even accidentally might be easy? &quot;I fight with forces 2, prime 2 and a gun&quot; is a very reasonable concept after all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11620,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","user":"twig","date":". 02-24-2019, 06:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-25T04:33:41-08:00","id":1291786,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1290802-mage-bloodbowl-op-starting-characters?p=1291625#post1291625\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> do we add the extra damage on top of the bullet's ordinary damage? I can't get a 100% clear answer from M20 currently.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, the Arete roll replaces the weapon's damage, with the to-hit roll's successes *not* adding to it. It just determines if the attack lands. Which is fine, really, given how powerful that is already. Forces would add +1 damage level, prime would make it aggravated.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 02-25-2019, 12:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-25T12:47:01-08:00","id":1291911,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1290802-mage-bloodbowl-op-starting-characters?p=1291786#post1291786\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, the Arete roll replaces the weapon's damage, with the to-hit roll's successes *not* adding to it. It just determines if the attack lands. Which is fine, really, given how powerful that is already. Forces would add +1 damage level, prime would make it aggravated.</div> </div> </div> </div>So 18 Aggravated damage for 3 quintessence (assuming 1 point per bullet, not one point for one turn's worth of attacks from a gun... could be 1 though), and 2 successes on an Arete roll? Assuming you got at least 1 success the turn before &quot;charging&quot; the bullets. And if you spend Willpower, we're looking at way more damage again.<br /> <br /> This isn't even that spec'd. Since the normal damage doesn't matter that much, you could hypothetically do this with Firearms 1, as long as you have enough to hit!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-25T21:01:30-08:00","id":1292062,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1290802-mage-bloodbowl-op-starting-characters?p=1291911#post1291911\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So 18 Aggravated damage for 3 quintessence (assuming 1 point per bullet, not one point for one turn's worth of attacks from a gun... could be 1 though), and 2 successes on an Arete roll?</div> </div> </div> </div>No. It's balanced rules-wise so that only the first bullet (i.e. the shot that you land and then do an Arete roll for - remember the Arete roll comes *after* the to-hit roll, and you only roll your own Arete once a round, time magick or not - does the Magickal damage. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> It's not quite 'realistic', yes. The only way around that is to turn the bullets into charms, which is a bit more involved.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-26T03:12:36-08:00","id":1292102,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1290802-mage-bloodbowl-op-starting-characters?p=1292062#post1292062\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No. It's balanced rules-wise so that only the first bullet (i.e. the shot that you land and then do an Arete roll for - remember the Arete roll comes *after* the to-hit roll, and you only roll your own Arete once a round, time magick or not - does the Magickal damage. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> It's not quite 'realistic', yes. The only way around that is to turn the bullets into charms, which is a bit more involved.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, I see. That's much better.<br /> <br /> So with 2 successes and 1 Willpower we're dealing a lethal amount of Aggravated damage (as in 7 or more) with a gunshot. But honestly... that's not so bad. In most forms of stories gunshots can be lethal. And serious foes will soak some of it of course.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11620,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","user":"twig","date":". 02-26-2019, 06:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-26T19:44:43-08:00","id":1292339,"title":"","content":"I'm not at all good with the Mage system, but what about someone who focuses on Prime and countering magic/ pulling the quintessence out of charms, and just uses mundane beat down's/ guns for mages that had relied on magic for their defenses/offences.<br /> Shotguns/Automatic rifles are pretty lethal without magical defenses.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16927-illithid","name":"Illithid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar16927_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-27T10:07:27-08:00","id":1292524,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Illithid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1290802-mage-bloodbowl-op-starting-characters?p=1292339#post1292339\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not at all good with the Mage system, but what about someone who focuses on Prime and countering magic/ pulling the quintessence out of charms, and just uses mundane beat down's/ guns for mages that had relied on magic for their defenses/offences.<br /> Shotguns/Automatic rifles are pretty lethal without magical defenses.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unweaving a spell takes as many successes as has been invested into it, that means that if the spell was a ritual (like Charms are) you most likely will need a Ritual to undo it. Zaping the Quintessence from a Mage or a Wonder can be temporarily inconvinient, but it's a magical action you weren't using to zap the enemy<br /> <br /> Basic Countermagic it's dificulty 7, you need all the Spheres involved in the spell at level 1 to counter, it's an action (it's similar to the Dodge action, meaning that you will have to divide your roll to do anything else), and doesn't work against stuff not casted at yourself.<br /> Offensive Countermagick allows for a more broad counter that includes the posibility of canceling effects casted at others and rebouncing the effect, but it has a greater difficulty (8 to cancel an effect casted to another target, 9 if you want to reflect it) - in general you have to be stronger than your enemy to pull it off.<br /> <br /> However...it may be possible to strengthen some of the Countermagick system by using Primium. Primium adds dice of Countermagick...implying that Arete + Primium dice could be used for active Countermagick. Also resisting using Innate Countermagick isn't an action, and thus you can cast a spell, shot a gun, or both while doing so.<br /> The build would be something like a cross between &quot;the Taser&quot; and a Hit-Mark<br /> <br /> <b>The Terminator</b><br /> Iteration X warmonger with enligthened military training<br /> <br /> <b>Attributes:</b><br /> Physical primary, with a focus on Dextrety because that\u00a1s what fire weapons use<br /> <br /> <b>Abilities:</b><br /> <br /> Firearms 5 / 4 freebies<br /> Athletics 5 / 4 freebies<br /> Conscience<br /> Alertness<br /> Stealth<br /> <br /> <b>Backgrounds:</b><br /> <br /> Enhancements 4 , Avatar 2, Requisitions 4, Arcane 5/ 12 freebies<br /> <br /> <b>Magick:</b><br /> Arete 3 /8 Freebies<br /> <br /> Prime 1, Forces 1, Life 1, Entropy 1, Mind 1, Matter 1<br /> <br /> We have 12 dots on Cybernetics :<br /> <br /> 10 dots. Primium Countermeasures. 5 extra dice of Countermagick<br /> 2 dots Skeletal Enhancement. It's mandatory, and 2 extra HP isn't bad<br /> <br /> This build uses Sphere levels at 1 for Countermagick but also to get bonuses. Entropy 1 it's particularly important for things like having a &quot;danger sense&quot; (to counter more effectively it could be combined with Prime 1 to have a general idea if the treath it's magical and what color of magick it is) and because it allows to find weak spots on the enemy defenses for extra accuracy and damage.<br /> Prime 2 was too tempting to make our shoots cause aggravated, but it may be better to leave it for the future since having all the important Spheres needed to counter magical attacks it's the basis of this build. With Prime as primary just 7xp will take us to that sweet spot. It can be Coincident (there's no difference between Agg and Lethal from the pov of normal humans, only magical healing and resistance it's impaired). In 8 aditional xp you can have Forces 2 to do trick shots and increase your naturaly decent damage by 1.<br /> <br /> 4 points of Permadox it's certainly crippling for a wizard (esp on the long run), but this build specializes low level Coincidental effects anyway, Paradox shouldn't be much of an issue.<br /> <br /> Requisitions 4 allows our cyborg to get pretty much any mundane weapon and amunition (on top of Devices) w/o needing complicated things like &quot;money&quot; or &quot;black market contacts&quot; that may be hard to mantain with high Arcane. Just let ol' Technocracy take care of it. After all, it's not like they will let you run free and have a private life with that much Primium anyway. A Biggs Mjollner Mk. IV causes better damage than a shotgun (10 dice) and military grade weapons can be circumstantially better<br /> <br /> With 5 dice of Innate Countermagick this build it's confy arround casters. While 8 dice (Primium + Arete) of Offensive Countermagick should be enough to counter most stuff not directed at you (as long as you have the Spheres), and dividing these between a counter and a shot may be doable. The build it's weak against being attacked with normal or supernatural claws or guns, but that can be solved requisitioning a good armor, and/or just being stealthy and not getting hit by surprise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 03-01-2019, 06:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-27T16:40:59-08:00","id":1292641,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1290802-mage-bloodbowl-op-starting-characters?p=1292524#post1292524\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>The Terminator</b><br /> Iteration X warmonger with enligthened military training</div> </div> </div> </div>This is really well done. But perhaps Matter 1 &gt; Mind 1 for this concept. With regards to resisting Mind effects, the high difficulty of using mind control on a Mage (Willpower + 3 for compelling mages) plus the effect of the Primium means you're already really well protected. Then again Mind 1 has all those buff effects. But Matter 1 is so useful if you're relying on tools like firearms and technology. Depends on preference.<br /> <br /> What Focus is allowing a cyborg to block magickal attacks against their allies, and bystanders?<br /> <br /> So a Reality Deviant throws a ball of lightning at someone; are we zapping it out of existence with a wired antenna, fizzling it out with a flick of psionic energy? Countermagick has fixed difficulties and isn't vulgar, but it's good to have an idea of how it fits into the wider Practice.<br /> <br /> Prime is also cool because Anti-Magick is a really great option for technocrats like this. Very fitting. The optional system allows you to make magick more difficult to pull off in general. You roll your Prime rating (2 in this case) against difficulty 8, and each success then costs a point of Quintessence. The result makes all magick for the scene +1 difficulty for each success. Reality is &quot;hardened&quot; through such a technique.<br /> <br /> My one final tweak would be that if this concept is meant to have holistic resistance, Avatar 5 is a must-have. Avatar gives some of the only soak against attacks made by spirits. With Avatar covering spirit attacks and Requisitions giving us the body armor to deal with normal attacks, this is all looking pretty impervious!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11620,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","user":"twig","date":". 02-27-2019, 07:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-28T06:39:39-08:00","id":1292749,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1290802-mage-bloodbowl-op-starting-characters?p=1292641#post1292641\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is really well done. But perhaps Matter 1 &gt; Mind 1 for this concept. With regards to resisting Mind effects, the high difficulty of using mind control on a Mage (Willpower + 3 for compelling mages) plus the effect of the Primium means you're already really well protected. Then again Mind 1 has all those buff effects. But Matter 1 is so useful if you're relying on tools like firearms and technology. Depends on preference.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a very good reasoning. I'm changing it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1290802-mage-bloodbowl-op-starting-characters?p=1292641#post1292641\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What Focus is allowing a cyborg to block magickal attacks against their allies, and bystanders?</div> </div> </div> </div>While the need of Focus to Countermagick was never very clear to me(it's magick alright, but it breaks so many normal casting rules, with it's difficulty and being a defensive action, that one can think it's instinctive), it is a very common requisite (Focus it's very thematic, I would require it). Also we may want to have the Primium embeded on it so we can better justify adding it to all our dicepools.<br /> <br /> A system of antenae sounds about right as they can be metalic and Weaves were always popular scientific hocus-pocus, SO: Since magick it's just wrong science fueled by genius, our cyborg body was built to generate a sub-sonic signal that blocks the special neuronal paths that connect the mind with the different enligthened sciences. This signal it's generated trough Primium filaments and ports located all around our body and connected to Primium retractable antenae for that extra effectivity, as anyone knows that Primium quantum vibrations block attempts to change reality. This Instrument, just for Countermagick, it's built trough our very hard to replace (and deadly to loose) Primium argumentations, and thus can count as Unique Specialized instrument to lower our difficulties on top of giving extra dice (Hey, if it uses Focus, it should have the advantages of Focus too)<br /> <br /> I think the antenae could be located at the head, they can't be used (actively, the passive protection needs no Focus) while wearing a helmet and give a very pinhead look when deployed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 02-28-2019, 09:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-28T18:10:03-08:00","id":1292894,"title":"","content":"<b>Immortal Phylactery Alchemist</b><br /> This one it's to milk for all it's worth the idea of Immortal Philactery Mage, with a greater elaboration and taking in count what has been said.<br /> I'm giving the stats first and latter the rationale<br /> <br /> This mage it's a practiced alchemist that blends occidental and oriental approaches with a ritual magick and a dash of modern understanding. Paradigm: Divine Order and Earthly Chaos Practices: Alchemy, High Ritual, Invigoration. Instruments: laboratory, internal alchemy, symbols, gestures, meditation, thought forms, ritual sword<br /> <br /> <b>Atributes:</b><br /> This build it's not very dependant on Attributes, but a good Stamina would help<br /> <br /> <b>Abilities:</b><br /> Science 4 (Chemistry) /2freebies<br /> Demolitions<br /> Technology<br /> Medicine<br /> Esoterica (Alchemy)<br /> Meditation<br /> Stealth<br /> Security<br /> <br /> <b>Backgrounds:</b><br /> Resources 2, Avatar 4 , Arcane 5 /4 freebies<br /> <br /> <b>Magick:</b><br /> Arete 3 /8 freebies<br /> Life 3, Matter 3, Correspondence 1 /7 freebies<br /> <br /> <b>Merits:</b><br /> Immortal / 7 freebies<br /> <br /> <b>Defects:</b><br /> Philactery -7 freebies (a titanium &amp; diamond ring or some other easy to carry and hideable item that can resist a lot)<br /> Psychic Vampire -5 freebies<br /> <br /> Immortal and Phylactery have several benefits that were mentioned above. How max that advantage?<br /> <br /> *One way it's to indulge in a type of damage that can be very dangerous for everyone but ain't going to *kill* you. Posion gas it's one of such as it kills mortals (and most mages) but can't easily obliterate your body even if you had to deploy it on proximity. Now, Matter it's somewhat unclear on the level that is required to transform relatively common substances into deadly gas BUT transmutation it's doable from level 2 and the only limit it's that you can't transform stuff into wildly different stuff. I've read a chemist say that Sarin gas and other chemical weapons were easily fabricable (by someone possesing great chemical knowledge), that non-ilegal stuff anyone can buy it's one or two steps from Sarin. I think it's fair to guess that if a mortal can make do with stuff that's one or two steps from the gas, a mage with matter 3 should do with stuff 5 or 10 steps away, perhaps more. Facilitating the production of the substance a great deal and making it pretty hard to follow trough conventional police investigation (like our Arcane 5 wasn't enough).<br /> More so, as can be read in the Awakening Substance section, Matter 2 can be used to <i>enhance </i>substances: Each success adds to the toxicity increasing the already great damage and the difficulty to resist by 1 per success (As an example for Sarin it's base 9 lethal per turn, non dodgeable, non resistable by armor that need 3 successes in Stamina diff 9 to resist). Note that Life can be used to resist, note that you *can* countermagick this if attempted (even if you're currently &quot;dead&quot;...and resisting magical poisons probably costs more than mundane ones).<br /> <br /> This kind of weapon would need time to be prepared but it's whole Coincident. In 7xp we will have Correspondence 2 that can be used to bring the dangerous cainsters using the glyphs on our really big pockets under our trenchcoat (seriously, if a mage has really big pockets, expect Correspondence :P ) or to directly teleport our gas to a closed room while we aren't there (you won't die otherwise, but it sure hurts). It's also useful to retrieve our Phylactery if stolen<br /> <br /> *Another way it's to do potshots and, as was suggested, this buld will have Arcane 5 that helps greatly with that. It's also one of the reasons for Life 3.<br /> <br /> Life can be used to kill in way that aren't dodgeable nor resistable with armor and can be very subtle and hard to pinpoint to the mage. If you think about it this mage can be VERY good at killing silently and making it appear an accident. Using tought forms and subtle gestures at someone that's drinking one cound use Life 3/Matter 2 to enhance the toxicity of the alcohol until a few pints equal death by overdose (not doable in combat). Using internal alchemy to incubate enhanced diseases would normaly be a very risky idea, but our body will recover from the worst. And directly killing trough Life 3 damage (internal wounds) it's hard to pinpoint, on top of not being dodgeable and avoiding most forms of Armor. Arcane 5 plus just being good at Stealth and Security will make sure no one connects you with the deaths.<br /> <br /> There are <i>things </i>that are harder to affect with Life, but Matter 3 has us mostly covered. Robots, machines, golems and several types of undead are paste unless they have some serious Prime, and even then they are paste if we get to build successes because they tough that we were dead. Bonus points because we can break most forms of mundane entombment and imprisonment (the bane of many immortals), and transmute stuff into silver for werewolves and cold iron for faes (not common treaths, but it doesnt hurt)<br /> <br /> *Life 2 can help to ignore pain<i>,</i>as to avoid becoming stuned by damage (the main reason why a good Stamina it's valuable for this build). The Phylactery takes care of the &quot;unconsciousness&quot; problem if our body refuses to function. We can overcome one focus, but at least 3 of the instruments of this build will be employable while dead: Though Forms (nothing to do buth think), Meditation (ok, you can't make the Lotus pose, but occidental phylosophical meditation needs no such thing) and Internal Alchemy (can keep working with the ecosistm of your dead body, as mumies know well). Arguably symbols written beforehand may keep their original function. That leaves only 3 instruments to overcome until you can cast while dead nearly as well as when you were alive<br /> <br /> Psychic Vampire was a difficult choice. It's a really crippling Defect that slowly hurts everything arround you, and drains your own life-force if you try to avoid it. It grants a -2 to difficulty to Life magicks for purposes of corruption, ilness or damage, but a +2 to healing and improvement effects (ouch!, and main reason for a strong Avatar. Getting a Sanctum/Node in the future would be golden to reduce ritual difs). However, it has a very unique property that I think could be a strong asset for the &quot;potshot&quot; strategy: &quot;Each health level you inflict on someone else with Life Sphere magick heals you of one health level if you\u2019re injured&quot;. So, you get a potshot and, if you want, raise from the dead (and if you don't want to do it yet, you can play dead with Stealth + Arcane or Life magicks). It also means, for a mage that cares little for pain, that you can heal in combat while causing damage in the same turn - nobody pulls that shit. Coupled with strong Matter-based Armor (and perhaps some painstakingly build Life enhancement) you can get a punch and keep going on top of your superb stealth-kill, even if you receive an instant death hit (the usual weakness of regeneration strategies)<br /> <br /> Now, this build surely could benefit from some Spheres: Mind 1 to avoid being mindrapped (and get some good boosts) would be really useful - so useful that I'm not sure if Matter 3 should be replaced with Matter 2/Mind 1, but buying a lvl 1 it's cheaper. Prime 1 for extra Quint and because Prime rocks. Forces for damage. No build yet has Spirit, and that means they're equally suceptible to Umbra based attacks. But nobody is perfect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 02-28-2019, 09:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-28T19:10:29-08:00","id":1292907,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1290802-mage-bloodbowl-op-starting-characters?p=1292641#post1292641\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is really well done. But perhaps Matter 1 &gt; Mind 1 for this concept.</div> </div> </div> </div>You' wouldn't choose mind over matter?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16927-illithid","name":"Illithid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar16927_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-01T02:31:06-08:00","id":1292973,"title":"","content":"Mind it's always a solid choice, but for &quot;the Terminator&quot; build Matter implies you can Countermagick attempts to tamper with your weapons. Since we depend on a good shotgun / weapon for damage it would be capital to not have the barrel melting or the powder refusing to ignite.<br /> <br /> Mind over Life could be a more reasonable choice for that build. Altrough that means we can't block healing and self-improvement, the bonuses and countering illusions and mind control over others could be worth it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-01T07:50:55-08:00","id":1293034,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Illithid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1290802-mage-bloodbowl-op-starting-characters?p=1292907#post1292907\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You' wouldn't choose mind over matter?</div> </div> </div> </div><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> very clever","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-01T07:55:49-08:00","id":1293036,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1290802-mage-bloodbowl-op-starting-characters?p=1292973#post1292973\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mind it's always a solid choice, but for &quot;the Terminator&quot; build Matter implies you can Countermagick attempts to tamper with your weapons. Since we depend on a good shotgun / weapon for damage it would be capital to not have the barrel melting or the powder refusing to ignite.<br /> <br /> Mind over Life could be a more reasonable choice for that build. Altrough that means we can't block healing and self-improvement, the bonuses and countering illusions and mind control over others could be worth it.</div> </div> </div> </div>It wouldn't be that crazy to simply take Prime 1, and then upgrade to Prime 2 when you have enough EXP. Very efficient, especially if Prime is Affinity. That way you can have all the level 1 spheres you need to countermagick significant effects.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-01T15:41:37-08:00","id":1293168,"title":"","content":"Again a very sensible argument. Lvl 2 ARE cheaper to buy than lvl 1. Changed!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-07T04:10:03-08:00","id":1294670,"title":"","content":"One-Shot<br /> <br /> tl;dr abusing broken Wonder rules to create a gun-wielding character who can one-shot anyone.<br /> <br /> Dexterity 5<br /> <br /> Firearms 5<br /> <br /> Gunsmithing 3+<br /> <br /> A uniquely designed and extremely well balanced gun made into a Forces 2 Prime 2 Wonder (Talisman) which fires Aggravated Bullets and amplifies their damage by accelerating them (hidden rail technology inside perhaps, micro-design based on hypertech). 2x the highest Sphere used means we're paying 4 background or freebie points for the Wonder. The Arete is 2, but by spending 8 more points we can get it up to 10. Yes, no sane ST would allow this, but it IS legal RAW.<br /> <br /> EDIT: There's no reason the gun can't also have an effect bound into it which means that it harms ghosts/spirits/etc that it hits, interacting with them via the spirit touch ability of Spirit 2. As far as I can tell this won't increase the cost of the Wonder, because the system for purchasing Wonders is completely broken.<br /> <br /> Gun killing someone in a single shot is 100% coincidental thanks to hollywood if nothing else. So 10 dice, difficulty 5, spending 1 Quintessence per shot for the Aggravated. 10 dice at difficulty 5 is 5 successes on average, which means 12 points of Aggravated damage as an AVERAGE, from a single shot simply hitting.<br /> <br /> Even if we reduce the Arete to 8 (something an ST is much more likely to allow, since &quot;gift from a true master of gunsmithing&quot; is more believable than &quot;an Oracle just gave me their gun&quot;) it's still going to be doing 10 Aggravated on average from a single shot.<br /> <br /> So that has cost us 12 Freebie points, plus 4 to reach Firearms 5 (can't risk missing of course).<br /> <br /> Now we just need to invest in the Node background so that the Wonder can recharge Quintessence when necessary, and also so that it can slowly lose Paradox on the off-chance it botches a shot (which could happen in a Sanctum, or a reality zone that still rejects guns, and could be very bad with a Sleeper witness).<br /> <br /> p.s. can a Mage spend their own Quintessence to reduce the difficulty of a roll made to use a Wonder?<br /> <br /> Spheres: Prime 2 means that you can make Charm bullets that automatically do Aggravated damage. This means you can continue to use the gun even if it runs out of Quintessence.<br /> <br /> Correspondence 2 with Matter 2 lets you make impossible shots, sending the bullet to your target without it being hampered by the intervening distance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11620,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","user":"twig","date":". 03-07-2019, 10:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-07T07:24:28-08:00","id":1294728,"title":"","content":"You could also use lvl 1 spheres to reduce the diff of the shot.<br /> <br /> About the ps, I also have this doubt. Never seen anywhere saying that you can or can't use quintessence to reduce wonder casting diff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-07T07:40:27-08:00","id":1294734,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1290802-mage-bloodbowl-op-starting-characters?p=1294728#post1294728\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You could also use lvl 1 spheres to reduce the diff of the shot.<br /> <br /> About the ps, I also have this doubt. Never seen anywhere saying that you can or can't use quintessence to reduce wonder casting diff.</div> </div> </div> </div>Reducing difficulty would be a great idea if the target is hard to hit, due to distance, small size etc.<br /> <br /> Also, something broken about the Wonder system is that making the Gun also have a Spirit 2 effect where it targets ghosts/spirits costs... nothing? Pretty sure it's nothing.<br /> <br /> And yes it would be good if someone could settle that, there must be something in M20 or Revised on that question.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-07T07:51:43-08:00","id":1294739,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1290802-mage-bloodbowl-op-starting-characters?p=1294734#post1294734\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, something broken about the Wonder system is that making the Gun also have a Spirit 2 effect where it targets ghosts/spirits costs... nothing? Pretty sure it's nothing.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not broken, you paid for a 2 dots wonder, then it can have up to 2 different effects.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-07T09:56:29-08:00","id":1294777,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1290802-mage-bloodbowl-op-starting-characters?p=1294739#post1294739\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's not broken, you paid for a 2 dots wonder, then it can have up to 2 different effects.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, but it's sort of weird that &quot;Gun that shoots for Aggravated Forces-enhanced damage&quot; is the same price as &quot;Gun that shoots for Aggravated Forces-enhanced damage, and can target spirits&quot;. Adding Sphere levels to an effect is free, essentially, as long as you don't raise the level of the highest Sphere.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-07T10:36:10-08:00","id":1294790,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1290802-mage-bloodbowl-op-starting-characters?p=1294777#post1294777\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, but it's sort of weird that &quot;Gun that shoots for Aggravated Forces-enhanced damage&quot; is the same price as &quot;Gun that shoots for Aggravated Forces-enhanced damage, and can target spirits&quot;. Adding Sphere levels to an effect is free, essentially, as long as you don't raise the level of the highest Sphere.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Actually, it's not free, you just wasn't taking everything you can with the points you spent. You paid for 2 powers and only got 1. That's one of the things I don't understand about examples of wonders in the books. They always doesn't have as much effects as they could, for a few exceptions..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}